.TH IMPROV-STREAM 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-stream \- Apply input edits from stdin and print the cells they change
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov stream\fR <db> <target\-measure>...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply input edits from stdin and print the cells they change.
.PP
One edit per line, MEASURE VALUE [Cat=Item,...] (the measure by id or name; no coordinate for a scalar measure). Each applies to a live incremental engine, and every changed cell of a target measure prints as MEASURE Cat=Item,... = VALUE. A malformed line is reported on stderr and skipped. At end of input the model is saved. Example: printf \*(AqPrice 12 Product=WidgetA\\n\*(Aq | improv stream m.db Revenue
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fItarget\-measure\fR>
The measures whose changes to print, by id or name
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1).
